---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Editorial standards — Gourmet Gastronomer"
  description="What makes a Gourmet Gastronomer page excellent, and what this encyclopedia refuses to be."
  permalink="/editorial/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Editorial standards", url: "/editorial/" }]}
>
  <main class="home" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow">Editorial</p>
    <h1>Editorial standards</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A page should make a careful reader more capable, not more impressed.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Gourmet Gastronomer is a food encyclopedia. It is not a recipe blog, a
        brand manifesto, or a search-engine article farm. If a paragraph could
        appear on any food website with the names swapped, it does not belong
        here.
      </p>
      <p>
        Developing pages should define the thing precisely, explain why it
        behaves, say what to notice, name the variables that change the outcome,
        and distinguish quality troubleshooting from food-safety guidance.
        Observation beats a kitchen timer except where a tested process time is
        the point.
      </p>
      <p>
        Important technical, historical, business, and safety claims need
        sources. Sensory judgments and recommendations should read as judgments,
        not as laws. We prefer primary and institutional sources; generic blogs
        are for discovery, not for canning times.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewed</strong> means a human has accepted the page. Agents
        may research, draft, and run checks. They do not certify the corpus.
        Incomplete work is labeled as a sketch.
      </p>
      <p>
        See also <a href="/method/">Method</a>,
        <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a>,
        <a href="/reuse/">Reuse</a>, and
        <a href="/catalog/sources/">Sources</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
